<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    "The Reckoning" — WEBWORK_EGG_RECKONING_QUEST_1.
    Design: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_egg_blackmarket_2026-09-24.md
    §2 (2a "the core quest", 2b "planting mechanics", 2d "discovery and
    consequences") and §3 (the hatch mechanism), S5 rulings 2/3/6/7.

    Full provenance for every node/field, checked live against the decompiled
    engine via RimSage this session (search_source/get_def_details), never
    guessed:
      QuestScriptDef fields, QuestNode_Sequence, GetMap(canBeSpace),
      GetSiteTile(preferCloserTiles), GetSitePartDefsByTagsAndFaction,
      GetDefaultSitePartsParams, SubScript(Util_AdjustPointsForDistantFight,
      Util_GenerateSite, Util_GetDefaultRewardValueFromPoints),
      SpawnWorldObjects, GeneratePawn(kindDef/faction), Delay(isQuestTimeout),
      Letter, Set, End(goodwillChangeAmount/goodwillChangeFactionOf/
      goodwillChangeReason/successHistoryEvent/failedOrExpiredHistoryEvent)
        src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Jawa_TheClaim.xml
        (site-generation shape) + Source/RimWorld/QuestGen/QuestNode_End.cs,
        QuestNode_GeneratePawn.cs (read in full this session)
      TradeRequest_RandomOfferDuration / TradeRequest_Initiate / GiveRewards
        src/RimUtinni/WildsteamEggBounty/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/
        RUT_WildsteamEggBounty.xml (same TradeRequestComp machinery, silver
        instead of eggs)
      SitePartDef Outpost (requiresFaction, minThreatPoints 300, tag Outpost)
        RimSage get_def_details "Outpost" (SitePartDef), read in full
      site.AllEnemiesDefeated — the real vanilla "the garrison is beaten"
      signal Sites already fire on their own (Site.CheckAllEnemiesDefeated),
      not invented
        Source/RimWorld/Planet/Site.cs:498 (read in full this session)
      PawnKindDefOf.Villager (the flavor "target" pawn — see below)
        Source/RimWorld/PawnKindDefOf.cs
      RM_QuestNode_GetHuttCartelSettlement / RM_QuestNode_EggPlantWatcher /
      RM_QuestNode_EggHatch — this mod's own Source/, see each file's header.

    THE THREE PATHS (§2a):
      1. Pay it yourself.  A TradeRequest of Silver to the Cartel's own
         settlement, ~2x the base reward (design's own "roughly 2x",
         INVENTED exact factor within it, same disclosure posture
         RUT_WildsteamEggBounty's own header already uses). Goodwill only —
         no thing reward (rewardValue forced to 0 before this branch's
         GiveRewards) — "the clean path spends the fee."
      2. Collect in person.  Defeat the outpost's garrison in the open
         (site.AllEnemiesDefeated — a REAL fight, the vanilla "all hostiles
         down or fled" signal). Standard reward, and -8 goodwill against the
         debtor's own faction (open, visible, "legal-adjacent, not
         deniable" per §2a) — INVENTED exact amount, disclosed.
         DISCLOSED MECHANISM GAP: the design calls this "vanilla
         shuttle/caravan-delivery machinery," but no such "deliver a captured
         pawn to a settlement" QuestNode exists (confirmed: no SendAway/Escort/
         Ransom/Bounty QuestNode or QuestScriptDef matches this shape). The
         debtor's fate (captured vs. killed in the fight) is left to the
         player's own combat, same as any other site assault — this is a
         real win condition, just not a literal captive-delivery mechanic.
      3. The egg.  RM_QuestNode_EggPlantWatcher watches for an RM_OllathrixEgg
         planted (roofed, unfogged, anywhere on the site map — see that
         node's own header for why not a single marked cell) while the site
         is undetected. Once planted, RM_QuestNode_EggHatch waits for the
         next night window (23:00-02:00, the design's own literal figure) or
         a small per-hour discovery chance (3%, INVENTED, disclosed),
         whichever comes first. Undiscovered hatch: Success, ZERO goodwill
         change (S5 ruling 6, total deniability). Discovered before hatch:
         Fail, -25 goodwill (the design's own already-stated ❓-25, carried
         forward as given). Both branches fire
         RUT_HistoryEvent_EggAssassination regardless of outcome (§2d).

    THE "TARGET": a flavor-only QuestNode_GeneratePawn (Villager, faction =
    $siteFaction), never spawned on the map. It exists so quest text can say
    [target_nameFull] and so QuestNode_End's goodwillChangeFactionOf — which
    reads a Thing's .Faction, not a Faction directly (Source/RimWorld/QuestGen/
    QuestNode_End.cs's own SlateRef<Thing> field, confirmed by reading it) —
    has something to point at. The debtor is not a placed, trackable
    individual; the outpost's whole garrison stands in for "his men," the
    same disclosed simplification path 2 already carries.

    Completion timer: randInt(10,15) days (the design's own ❓10-15 range,
    used as given, not re-invented) after acceptance — Fail ("the target
    learns and flees") if none of the three paths lands first. Offer window
    (expireDaysRange) 4~8, this campaign's own quest-family convention.

    Two concrete leaves inherit this same tree (skill §3: ParentName inherits
    the whole root and text packs) so the family can fire both from the
    Cartel trader (route 3, primary, per skill §7) AND, separately, as a rare
    natural-pool fallback (route 1) for a colony that never meets the trader
    — a single def cannot do both: vanilla's own givenBy+randomlySelectable
    idiom (Data/Odyssey/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Script_AlphaThrumboSighting.xml,
    confirmed via search_source) turns OFF the natural pool.
  -->

  <QuestScriptDef Abstract="True" Name="RUT_Reckoning">
    <expireDaysRange>4~8</expireDaysRange>
    <defaultChallengeRating>2</defaultChallengeRating>
    <everAcceptableInSpace>true</everAcceptableInSpace>

    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->The Reckoning of Debts</li>
        <li>questName->A Cartel Reckoning</li>
        <li>questName->[cartelFaction_name]'s Reckoning</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>

    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->[cartelFaction_name] controls the door off-world and the water on the way to it. [target_nameDef], of [siteFaction_name], owes them a debt and will not pay. The Cartel wants it closed — how is your business.
\n\nThree ways to close it: hand the Cartel the silver yourself (roughly [payAmount_money]); go to [target_pronoun]'s outpost and settle it in the open, at the cost of [siteFaction_name]'s goodwill; or carry an ollathrix egg in and leave it somewhere undetected. It hatches in the night. No one need ever know how [target_nameDef] died — except you.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>

    <root Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
      <nodes>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SubScript">
          <def>Util_AdjustPointsForDistantFight</def>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetMap">
          <canBeSpace>true</canBeSpace>
        </li>

        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.EggReckoning.RM_QuestNode_GetHuttCartelSettlement">
          <maxTileDistance>80</maxTileDistance>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetSiteTile">
          <storeAs>siteTile</storeAs>
          <preferCloserTiles>true</preferCloserTiles>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetSitePartDefsByTagsAndFaction">
          <storeAs>sitePartDefs</storeAs>
          <storeFactionAs>siteFaction</storeFactionAs>
          <sitePartsTags>
            <li>
              <tag>Outpost</tag>
            </li>
          </sitePartsTags>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GeneratePawn">
          <storeAs>target</storeAs>
          <kindDef>Villager</kindDef>
          <faction>$siteFaction</faction>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetDefaultSitePartsParams">
          <tile>$siteTile</tile>
          <faction>$siteFaction</faction>
          <sitePartDefs>$sitePartDefs</sitePartDefs>
          <storeSitePartsParamsAs>sitePartsParams</storeSitePartsParamsAs>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SubScript">
          <def>Util_GenerateSite</def>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SpawnWorldObjects">
          <worldObjects>$site</worldObjects>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SubScript">
          <def>Util_GetDefaultRewardValueFromPoints</def>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>baseReward</name>
          <value>$rewardValue</value>
        </li>

        <!-- ❓ design's own "roughly 2x"; INVENTED exact factor within it. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>payAmount</name>
          <value>$(round(baseReward * randFloat(1.8, 2.2)))</value>
        </li>

        <!-- ❓ design's own 10-15 day range for the completion timer, used as given. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_Delay">
          <delayTicks>$(randInt(10,15)*60000)</delayTicks>
          <isQuestTimeout>true</isQuestTimeout>
          <outSignalComplete>ReckoningTimeout</outSignalComplete>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
          <inSignal>ReckoningTimeout</inSignal>
          <label>Quest expired: [resolvedQuestName]</label>
          <text>[target_nameDef] has heard enough rumours to move on. The debt stands, uncollected.</text>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>ReckoningTimeout</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>

        <!-- Path 1: pay it yourself. Goodwill only, no thing reward. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_TradeRequest_RandomOfferDuration">
          <settlement>$cartelSettlement</settlement>
          <storeAs>payTimeout</storeAs>
          <storeEstimatedTravelTimeAs>payTravelTime</storeEstimatedTravelTimeAs>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>payThing</name>
          <value>Silver</value>
          <convertTo>ThingDef</convertTo>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_TradeRequest_Initiate">
          <settlement>$cartelSettlement</settlement>
          <requestedThingDef>$payThing</requestedThingDef>
          <requestedThingCount>$payAmount</requestedThingCount>
          <duration>$payTimeout</duration>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>rewardValue</name>
          <value>0</value>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GiveRewards">
          <inSignal>cartelSettlement.TradeRequestFulfilled</inSignal>
          <parms>
            <allowGoodwill>true</allowGoodwill>
          </parms>
          <useDifficultyFactor>false</useDifficultyFactor>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>cartelSettlement.TradeRequestFulfilled</inSignal>
          <outcome>Success</outcome>
          <sendStandardLetter>true</sendStandardLetter>
        </li>

        <!-- Path 2: collect in person — a real fight, open and visible. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>rewardValue</name>
          <value>$baseReward</value>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GiveRewards">
          <inSignal>site.AllEnemiesDefeated</inSignal>
          <parms>
            <allowGoodwill>true</allowGoodwill>
            <thingRewardRequired>true</thingRewardRequired>
          </parms>
          <useDifficultyFactor>false</useDifficultyFactor>
        </li>
        <!-- ❓ INVENTED goodwill penalty, disclosed. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>site.AllEnemiesDefeated</inSignal>
          <outcome>Success</outcome>
          <sendStandardLetter>true</sendStandardLetter>
          <goodwillChangeAmount>-8</goodwillChangeAmount>
          <goodwillChangeFactionOf>$target</goodwillChangeFactionOf>
          <goodwillChangeReason>RUT_HistoryEvent_ReckoningAbduction</goodwillChangeReason>
        </li>

        <!-- Path 3: the egg. The one C# verb. -->
        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.EggReckoning.RM_QuestNode_EggPlantWatcher">
          <site>$site</site>
          <inSignalEnable>site.MapGenerated</inSignalEnable>
          <outSignalPlanted>EggPlanted</outSignalPlanted>
          <outSignalDiscovered>EggDiscovered</outSignalDiscovered>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
          <inSignal>EggDiscovered</inSignal>
          <label>They've seen you</label>
          <text>Someone at [target_nameDef]'s outpost has spotted trouble. Whatever happens now, it will not be quiet.</text>
        </li>

        <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.EggReckoning.RM_QuestNode_EggHatch">
          <site>$site</site>
          <inSignalEnable>EggPlanted</inSignalEnable>
          <outSignalHatched>EggHatched</outSignalHatched>
          <outSignalFoundBeforeHatch>EggFoundBeforeHatch</outSignalFoundBeforeHatch>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_Set">
          <name>rewardValue</name>
          <value>$baseReward</value>
        </li>
        <li Class="QuestNode_GiveRewards">
          <inSignal>EggHatched</inSignal>
          <parms>
            <allowGoodwill>true</allowGoodwill>
            <thingRewardRequired>true</thingRewardRequired>
          </parms>
          <useDifficultyFactor>false</useDifficultyFactor>
        </li>
        <!-- S5 ruling 6: total deniability — no goodwillChangeAmount at all. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>EggHatched</inSignal>
          <outcome>Success</outcome>
          <sendStandardLetter>true</sendStandardLetter>
          <successHistoryEvent>RUT_HistoryEvent_EggAssassination</successHistoryEvent>
        </li>

        <!-- ❓ design's own already-stated -25, used as given. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>EggFoundBeforeHatch</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
          <sendStandardLetter>true</sendStandardLetter>
          <goodwillChangeAmount>-25</goodwillChangeAmount>
          <goodwillChangeFactionOf>$target</goodwillChangeFactionOf>
          <goodwillChangeReason>RUT_HistoryEvent_ReckoningAttempt</goodwillChangeReason>
          <failedOrExpiredHistoryEvent>RUT_HistoryEvent_EggAssassination</failedOrExpiredHistoryEvent>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_End">
          <inSignal>map.MapRemoved</inSignal>
          <outcome>Fail</outcome>
        </li>

      </nodes>
    </root>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <!-- Route 3 (skill §7): the Cartel hands you the contract while you browse.
       ❓ DISCLOSED: vanilla's givenBy tag is generic to ALL traders
       (Traders/OrbitalScanner/Reading/Beggars — confirmed via search_source,
       no per-TraderKindDef filter exists), so this is a generic-trader offer
       with Cartel framing in the text, not a literal Cartel-only gate. -->
  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_Reckoning">
    <defName>RUT_Reckoning_CartelOffer</defName>
    <givenBy>
      <li>Traders</li>
    </givenBy>
    <randomlySelectable>false</randomlySelectable>
    <rootMinPoints>300</rootMinPoints>
  </QuestScriptDef>

  <!-- Route 1 (skill §7): rare natural-pool fallback for a colony that never
       meets the trader. rootMinPoints 300 matches Outpost's own
       minThreatPoints exactly (RimSage-confirmed), not arbitrary.
       ❓ minRefireDays/rootSelectionWeight INVENTED within shipped ranges
       (0.15-2.0), disclosed. -->
  <QuestScriptDef ParentName="RUT_Reckoning">
    <defName>RUT_Reckoning_Rumor</defName>
    <rootSelectionWeight>0.15</rootSelectionWeight>
    <rootMinPoints>300</rootMinPoints>
    <minRefireDays>30</minRefireDays>
  </QuestScriptDef>

</Defs>
